.TH doubletake-test-receiver 1 "August 2026" "doubletake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doubletake-test-receiver \- diagnostic AirPlay mirroring receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doubletake-test-receiver
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doubletake-test-receiver
is a local AirPlay receiver for testing the real
.B doubletake
sender without an Apple TV or other receiver. It performs pairing, RTSP session
setup, timing, event, video, and audio protocol handling, then drains incoming
media while reporting activity statistics.
.PP
It is a diagnostic sink, not a media player: it does not display video or play
audio. By default it listens only on the IPv4 loopback address.
.SH PROTOCOL COVERAGE AND LIMITATIONS
The profiles exercise independent pairing, SETUP-order, timing, FairPlay, and
audio-layout combinations observed across first- and third-party receivers.
.PP
Profile names select synthetic receiver-side validation presets only. The
sender does not branch on those names, or on the advertised receiver name,
model, manufacturer, or an exact feature-mask fingerprint. It selects behavior
from advertised capabilities, receiver implementation version where necessary,
and the protocol that actually completes.
.PP
The sender always starts with the control-only SETUP sequence. A fixture which
explicitly rejects that control shape
exercises one bounded transition to legacy media-first SETUP. Feature 59 affects
only the initial audio descriptor: it selects
.BR streamConnections ;
its absence selects
.BR controlPort .
An explicit descriptor rejection permits one alternate-shape retry.
.PP
Encrypted HAP sessions use descriptor-only FairPlay keys. Plaintext/raw sessions
use available root FairPlay keys on control and media SETUP. NTP and PTP use the
same presentation-latency policy; only their network-clock representation
differs.
A nonzero screen-audio mask advertising neither ALAC nor AAC-ELD is rejected
when audio is enabled;
.B \-no-audio
keeps pairing, timing, control, and video available.
.PP
The modern profile omits display metadata from pre-session
.BR /info ,
then returns ordinary receiver information under the control SETUP response's
.B info
key when
.B combinedGetInfoWithControlSetup
is requested without a qualifier. This validates that the sender starts its
encoder from the session-time nominal canvas, while treating separately
advertised maximum dimensions only as an acceptance ceiling.
.PP
It parses the outer AirPlay video framing and counts video and audio traffic.
The AppleTV3 and UxPlay profiles authenticate the FairPlay key, decrypt legacy
AES-CTR video, and validate AVCC/NAL framing. It does not decode or display
video or play audio; other encrypted media paths remain transport-only checks.
This program is a diagnostic sink, not a media player or a
receiver-compatibility substitute.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B roku
Advertise third-party/HKP pairing, PTP feature 41 with implementation version
377.40.x, feature 59 absent, ALAC, and no FPSAP. It rejects the initial control
SETUP to verify the single media-first transition and the narrow versioned NTP
selection. Under authenticated HAP, the fixture rejects the initial
.B controlPort
audio shape and verifies the sender's single bounded
.B streamConnections
retry. This is the default.
.TP
.B modern
Advertise CoreUtils HomeKit-style pairing, features 41 and 59, FPSAP, ALAC, and
full PTP clock metadata. It verifies encrypted control and event channels,
acceptance of the initial control SETUP, descriptor-only FairPlay keys, and a
.B streamConnections
audio descriptor. Pre-session
.B /info
omits displays; combined control SETUP info supplies a 1920x1080 nominal canvas
and a distinct 3840x2160 maximum.
.TP
.B lg
Advertise third-party/HKP HAP, feature-41 PTP with a working implementation
version, feature 59 absent, and ALAC. It verifies encrypted control with
one rejected control SETUP followed by media-first SETUP, a ChaCha key alongside
the legacy audio control port, and the compatibility fallback which anchors a
receiver ClockID locally when Apple's private PTP headers are absent. That
fallback assumes the receiver uses the sender's numeric boot-clock phase; it is
not equivalent to participating in a PTP clock domain.
.TP
.B appletv3
Advertise raw pairing with feature 27, FPSAP, ALAC, and no PTP or feature 59. It
rejects the initial control SETUP and verifies the one media-first transition,
receiver-initiated NTP, the original raw FairPlay derivation, and plaintext
root-level FairPlay keys.
.TP
.B uxplay
Advertise raw pairing without feature 27, which verifies
.B X-Apple-PD
FairPlay-secret mixing, media-first NTP, ALAC, and an omitted optional
.B eventPort
in every SETUP response. It rejects the initial control SETUP to exercise the
one media-first transition and validates plaintext root FairPlay keys.
.TP
.B airserver
Advertise CoreUtils-like pairing capabilities but reject the HAP probe, which
verifies the bounded raw-pairing fallback without identity matching. It also
advertises feature 59 and only AAC-ELD screen audio, and verifies control-first
SETUP by accepting the initial control request. Its plaintext feature-59
.B streamConnections
descriptor is rejected once and the alternate
.B controlPort
form is accepted. It also verifies sender-initiated NTP through the returned
timing port and plaintext root-level FairPlay keys. The profile name
.B airtame
is accepted as an alias. The sender's AAC-ELD encoder is optional; install the
.B libfdk-aac
development files and build it with
.B CGO_ENABLED=1 go build \-tags fdk_aac \-o bin/doubletake ./cmd/doubletake
when testing audio with this profile. A normal build can exercise its video and
control path with
.BR \-no-audio .
.SH AUTHENTICATION
All authenticated modes use the single value supplied by
.B \-code
or
.BR DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE .
The environment variable takes precedence over the command-line option.
.TP
.B none
Allow transient pairing and do not challenge RTSP requests. A code must not be
supplied. This is the default.
.TP
.B pin
Advertise PIN-required pairing and use the code for SRP pair-setup. A
.B /pair-pin-start
request prints the configured code in the receiver log. RTSP Digest
authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B password
Use the code as the configured SRP pairing password without advertising an
on-screen PIN. RTSP Digest authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B digest
Allow transient pairing, then require RFC 2069 Digest authentication for media
session requests using the configured code.
.TP
.B combined
Use the code as a configured fixed password and require subsequent RTSP Digest
authentication. Fixtures using the legacy/HKP pairing flow also consume it
during SRP pair-setup; CoreUtils/HAP fixtures pair transiently and reserve it
for Digest. This mode does not advertise or display an on-screen PIN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-listen \fIADDRESS\fR
TCP listen address for the AirPlay control connection. The default is
.BR 127.0.0.1:7000 .
Port 0 requests an ephemeral port; the actual bound address is printed at
startup.
.TP
.B \-profile \fIPROFILE\fR
Receiver-side validation preset: \fBmodern\fR, \fBroku\fR, \fBlg\fR,
\fBappletv3\fR, \fBuxplay\fR, or \fBairserver\fR. The default is
.BR roku .
.TP
.B \-auth \fIMODE\fR
Authentication mode: \fBnone\fR, \fBpin\fR, \fBpassword\fR, \fBdigest\fR, or
.BR combined .
The default is \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-code \fICODE\fR
Unified pairing and/or Digest code selected by
.BR \-auth .
Authenticated modes require a non-empty code. Prefer the environment variable
to avoid exposing the value in shell history and
.BR ps (1)
output.
.TP
.B \-name \fINAME\fR
Receiver name advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value uses the selected profile's default.
.TP
.B \-model \fIMODEL\fR
Receiver model advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value uses the selected profile's default.
.TP
.B \-device-id \fIIDENTIFIER\fR
Receiver device ID advertised by
.BR /info .
An empty value generates a random locally administered identifier for this
process.
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable verbose receiver protocol logging.
.TP
.B \-stats-interval \fIDURATION\fR
Print periodic protocol and media statistics using a Go duration such as
\fB1s\fR or \fB500ms\fR. Zero disables periodic output. Final statistics are
always printed.
.TP
.B \-h, \-help
Show command-line help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE
Pairing/password/Digest code. When set, including to an empty value, it takes
precedence over
.BR \-code .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the default Roku-profile receiver with a configured pairing password:
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE=testpass doubletake-test-receiver \-profile roku \-auth password
.TP
Connect a synthetic sender using that password:
.B DOUBLETAKE_CODE=testpass doubletake \-target 127.0.0.1 \-port 7000 \-test
.TP
Exercise modern pairing and Digest authentication with one shared fixed
password (no on-screen PIN):
.B DOUBLETAKE_RECEIVER_CODE=4827 doubletake-test-receiver \-profile modern \-auth combined \-stats-interval 2s
.TP
Run an unauthenticated receiver on an ephemeral port:
.B doubletake-test-receiver \-listen 127.0.0.1:0
.PP
Copy the printed
.I PORT
into the sender invocation:
.IP
.B doubletake \-target 127.0.0.1 \-port PORT \-test
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR doubletake (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Omar Roth.
